On Sun, Mar 21, 2010 at 2:10 PM, Luke Bergen <lukeabergen@gmail.com> wrote:
> Hmm, tenses used as tcita have confused me for this reason.  So, as a
> followup question, {broda pu lo nu brode} means "broda and then brode" or
> "broda but first brode"?  Does PU when used as a tcita mark the main bridi
> or the following sumti and what is it's "origin"?

 pu broda = broda pu (ku) = broda pu zo'e = lo nu broda cu purci (zo'e)

 broda pu lo nu brode = lo nu broda cu purci lo nu brode

This works the same for BAIs:

 mu'i broda = broda mu'i (ku) = broda mu'i zo'e = lo nu broda cu se mukti (zo'e)

 broda mu'i lo nu brode = lo nu broda cu se mukti lo nu brode

Notice that "pu" = "fi'o purci", while "mu'i" = "fi'o se mukti".

